# The SFTP plugin's test server (R25 commit 76; answer 99): OpenSSH's own
# sshd, started and stopped by the plugin's container tests themselves,
# as the container's ordinary user, on a loopback port only, so nothing
# listens outside the container or the runner.
#
# The tests fill in every @NAME@: a fresh folder of their own, a free
# port, the user, the case's sign-in lines, the SFTP subsystem and any
# extra lines. The host key, the client key and the password are made at
# test time, in that folder or by run-tests.sh, and never committed.

ListenAddress 127.0.0.1
Port @PORT@
HostKey @DIR@/host_ed25519
PidFile @DIR@/sshd.pid
AuthorizedKeysFile @DIR@/authorized_keys
AllowUsers @USER@
PermitRootLogin no
# The folder is the test's own, under the container's /tmp.
StrictModes no
UsePAM yes
PrintMotd no
PrintLastLog no
X11Forwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
PermitTTY no
LogLevel ERROR

# The case's sign-in methods.
@AUTH@

# The case's extra lines: a noisy shell startup file, a try limit.
@EXTRA@

Subsystem sftp @SUBSYSTEM@
